---
import Diagram from '../Diagram.astro';
---
<Diagram caption="The remote-access direction the same architecture opens up — not something we have deployed. Landing a roaming user on the nearest Secure Access region removes the trip back to a fixed concentrator, which is the part that hurts when the user and the resource are both a long way from headquarters.">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 214" role="img" aria-labelledby="raTitle raDesc">
    <title id="raTitle">Possible future remote access: nearest Secure Access region instead of a fixed VPN concentrator</title>
    <desc id="raDesc">
      A possible future path: a roaming user in APAC connects to the nearest Cisco Secure
      Access region, crosses the Secure Access backbone, and reaches the resource by the
      geographically appropriate path. Shown beneath it, dimmed, is the pattern it avoids:
      the same user tunnelling back to a VPN concentrator in New York only to return to a
      resource in APAC.
    </desc>

    <text class="panel-title" x="14" y="26">POSSIBLE DIRECTION — NEAREST-REGION REMOTE ACCESS</text>

    <rect class="node-edge" x="14" y="38" width="150" height="50" rx="8" />
    <text class="label" x="28" y="60">Roaming user</text>
    <text class="sub" x="28" y="77">in APAC</text>

    <path class="link-standby" d="M164 63 L200 63" />
    <path class="link-standby" d="M192 57 L200 63 L192 69" />

    <rect class="node-edge" x="208" y="38" width="150" height="50" rx="8" />
    <text class="label" x="222" y="60">Nearest Secure</text>
    <text class="label" x="222" y="78">Access region</text>

    <path class="link-standby" d="M358 63 L394 63" />
    <path class="link-standby" d="M386 57 L394 63 L386 69" />

    <rect class="node-edge" x="402" y="38" width="150" height="50" rx="8" />
    <text class="label" x="416" y="60">Secure Access</text>
    <text class="label" x="416" y="78">backbone</text>

    <path class="link-standby" d="M552 63 L588 63" />
    <path class="link-standby" d="M580 57 L588 63 L580 69" />

    <rect class="node-edge" x="596" y="38" width="150" height="50" rx="8" />
    <text class="label" x="610" y="60">Resource by the</text>
    <text class="label" x="610" y="78">closest path</text>

    <!-- what it avoids -->
    <text class="panel-title" x="14" y="136">WHAT IT AVOIDS — TROMBONING TO A FIXED CONCENTRATOR</text>

    <rect class="node" x="14" y="148" width="180" height="50" rx="8" />
    <text class="sub" x="28" y="170">Roaming user</text>
    <text class="sub" x="28" y="187">in APAC</text>

    <path class="link-dim" d="M194 173 L282 173" />
    <path class="link-dim" d="M274 167 L282 173 L274 179" />

    <rect class="node" x="290" y="148" width="180" height="50" rx="8" />
    <text class="sub" x="304" y="170">VPN concentrator</text>
    <text class="sub" x="304" y="187">in New York</text>

    <path class="link-dim" d="M470 173 L558 173" />
    <path class="link-dim" d="M550 167 L558 173 L550 179" />

    <rect class="node" x="566" y="148" width="180" height="50" rx="8" />
    <text class="sub" x="580" y="170">Resource back</text>
    <text class="sub" x="580" y="187">in APAC</text>
  </svg>
</Diagram>
